"MK2a LAWS over a literal carrier with the compile`s records. V is exactly: the two rows giving p1 two Names (uniqueness within Person has Name); the two joined rows giving p2 and p3 one Name and Age (the external uniqueness); p4, who has no Age (the explicit mandatory); the reflexive row (irreflexive) and the three rows the asymmetric ring breaks, not the row whose reverse is absent; and p4 again, happy with no Age (the subset). The disjunctive mandatory holds, since every Person is happy or likes some Person. The subset with a join recipe and the prohibited deontic are listed as unbuilt. The instance reflection, not yet booted, holds p4 an instance of Person and most specifically so, Ann one of Name, and p1 none of Name. The schema reflected: Person has Name has its primary reading rPersonHasName and its roles are used in it; Person has PersonId, named in state:mapinputs alone, is declared with its roles and players; Person has Age has no third role. The involvement link Person is involved in Person likes Person, named in state:mapinputs alone with no template, has its reading with NORMA`s text and its Predicate; Person has PersonId, templated in state:schemereadings, gets no minted text.",
